 "design": "R6 whether the interval needs the normality the generator hands it.\n\nDesign fixed before running (2026-09-16, written 14:50 EDT). Every coverage simulation in this paper\ndraws its latent run effects from a multivariate normal. Benchmark scores are averages over thousands of\nbinary or near-binary items, so normality is a reasonable working assumption, and it is still an\nassumption the paper never tests. Seed effects on a small benchmark could be heavy-tailed, and recipes\nplainly differ in how variable their runs are, since a recipe that trains on a narrow corpus has more\nroom to move between seeds than one that trains on a broad mixture.\nThis run breaks both assumptions on purpose. It draws the latent effects from a multivariate t with 3, 5\nand 10 degrees of freedom, scaled so the covariance is unchanged, and it separately gives the 25 recipes\nvariance scales spread over a four-fold and a sixteen-fold range while holding the average fixed. It then\nscores the same four intervals at 4,000 replicates per cell. An interval that holds near nominal under a\nt with three degrees of freedom, which has no finite kurtosis, is an interval a reader can use on real\nscores. Seed 20260961 keeps the draws distinct.\n",
